The function is already tiny; the only wins are making the valid path a predictable fall-through and loading the profile pointer once, so I used `__builtin_expect` to tell the compiler the bounds/null failure is the unlikely branch.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```